# Why this Module's primary service carries no `healthcheck:`.
# A marker with no justification is a silent skip in file form; lint-config
# refuses an empty one.

The pinned image otel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib:0.160.0 is distroless:
`sh` is not on its PATH and it ships no HTTP client, verified 2026-09-07. A
Docker healthcheck has nothing to execute. This is the one Module whose smoke
check already proves the thing a healthcheck would only approximate:
services/otel-collector/smoke.sh posts a real trace, log line and metric over
OTLP from the host and then reads all three back out of Tempo, Loki and
Prometheus. The health_check extension is deliberately not enabled — it would
add a port to publish and still need a client inside the container to poll it.
